msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid "We're pleased to announce the release of Quarkus 3.35."
msgstr ""

msgid "This release brings several notable features:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/53295[#53295] - JAR tree-shaking "
"to eliminate unused classes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/53278[#53278] - Profile-Guided "
"Optimization (PGO) support for native builds"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/53339[#53339] - Semeru AOT support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/51063[#51063] - Support "
"`@Transactional` for Hibernate Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/53432[#53432] - CORS support for "
"the management interface"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/52919[#52919] - Remove the use of "
"System Properties to propagate configuration in tests"
msgstr ""

msgid "New snapshot distribution infrastructure"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.35, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.35."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your "
"applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/"
"Migration-Guide-3.35[Quarkus 3.35 migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "JAR tree-shaking"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A new experimental `quarkus.package.jar.tree-shake.mode` option enables "
"build-time dependency tree-shaking.\n"
"When set to `classes`, Quarkus performs bytecode reachability analysis to "
"identify and exclude unused classes from runtime dependencies, reducing "
"application JAR size."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The analysis traces references through supertypes, annotations, "
"`ServiceLoader` entries, reflective class loading, and more."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As an example, running tree-shaking on the Quarkus CLI removes over 6,000 "
"unreachable classes, saving around 18 MB (39.5%)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature supports `fast-jar`, `uber-jar`, `legacy-jar`, and `aot-jar` "
"packaging types."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As mentioned, this new feature is experimental, and feedback is highly "
"welcome!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Profile-guided optimization for native builds"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can now opt in to Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO) for native builds by "
"setting `quarkus.native.pgo.enabled=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that PGO is a feature of Oracle GraalVM and is not available in GraalVM "
"Community Edition."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When enabled, Quarkus uses your integration tests as the workload to profile "
"the application.\n"
"The resulting PGO data is then fed into the native compilation for better "
"runtime performance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The implementation follows a similar pattern to the Project Leyden AOT "
"support introduced in Quarkus 3.32."
msgstr ""

msgid "Semeru AOT support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Building on the Project Leyden AOT integration from Quarkus 3.32, Quarkus "
"now also supports IBM Semeru's AOT features."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In initial testing on the `rest-json` quickstart with IBM Semeru Runtime "
"Open Edition 25, startup time was cut roughly in half (from ~380 ms down to "
"~190 ms)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For now, this is limited to building JARs with Semeru AOT, automatic "
"container image building (as available with Leyden) is not yet supported."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@Transactional</code> for Hibernate Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus now supports the `@Transactional` annotation for Hibernate Reactive, "
"thanks to a new `quarkus-reactive-transactions` extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This means you can use the familiar `@Transactional` annotation on methods "
"that return `Uni`, and the transaction lifecycle (begin, commit, rollback) "
"will be managed within the reactive pipeline."
msgstr ""

msgid "A few things to keep in mind:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only `TxType.REQUIRED` is currently supported."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mixing `@Transactional` with `@WithTransaction` or `@WithSessionOnDemand` is "
"not allowed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Methods annotated with `@Transactional` are no longer automatically "
"considered `@Blocking`. If your method is blocking but returns `Uni`, you "
"now need an explicit `@Blocking` annotation. See the https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.35[migration guide] for details."
msgstr ""

msgid "CORS support for the management interface"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The management interface now has its own dedicated CORS configuration, "
"allowing you to set CORS policies independently from the main HTTP interface."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The test infrastructure no longer uses System Properties to propagate "
"configuration from Dev Services, Test Resources, and Test Profiles.\n"
"This change opens the door for better parallel test execution (which we hope "
"to achieve at some point in the future) and makes the Config system truly "
"immutable."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tests using `QuarkusDevModeTest`, `QuarkusIntegrationTest`, or "
"`QuarkusMainIntegrationTest` can now declare a `Config` field or method "
"parameter to access the updated configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "New snapshot distribution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus snapshots are no longer published to Sonatype, which had reliability "
"issues with the volume of artifacts involved.\n"
"Snapshots are now published daily as GitHub Releases in the https://github."
"com/quarkusio/quarkus-ecosystem-ci/releases[quarkusio/quarkus-ecosystem-ci] "
"repository, with version `999-SNAPSHOT`.\n"
"Each release contains a `maven-repo.tar.gz` asset with pre-built Maven "
"artifacts that you can extract into your local Maven repository."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For CI setups, a dedicated https://github.com/quarkusio/install-quarkus-"
"snapshots-action/[GitHub Action] is also available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More details can be found in the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/"
"main/CONTRIBUTING.md#using-snapshots[Using snapshots] section of the "
"contributing guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Jackson reflection-free serializers for Quarkus REST"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We initially planned to make Jackson reflection-free serializers the default "
"for Quarkus REST in 3.35.\n"
"However, thanks to several community members who tested this feature and "
"reported issues, we identified a number of edge cases that still need to be "
"addressed.\n"
"We decided to postpone making it the default to 3.36, so that we can fix "
"these issues first."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We are very grateful to everyone who took the time to report problems, your "
"feedback is what makes Quarkus better."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the meantime, we very much welcome more testing from our community.\n"
"You can enable reflection-free serializers by adding the following property "
"to your configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Please report any issues you encounter on https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/issues[GitHub]."
msgstr ""

